{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FindHamiltonianPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only subtrees with no solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left with too few"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usable neighbours), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Hamiltonian.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Hamiltonian.swift#L580"},"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"hamiltonianPath()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE15hamiltonianPath5Walks0E0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgyF","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text"